    "description": "Mineral Specimen Lot - 3 Pieces\nColemanite, Aquamarine Beryl, Pink Dolomite\nVintage, Late 20th Century\nA curated collection of three distinct geological specimens, each housed in a protective acrylic display case. This lot features specimens with specific regional significance, including pieces from historic mining locations. These minerals are ideal for geology enthusiasts, educators, or collectors of natural history specimens.\nItems Included:\nColemanite Specimen: Translucent crystal formation sourced from Death Valley, mounted on yellow felt.\nAquamarine Beryl: Large raw specimen dug from the mine dump at Beryl Mountain, South Acworth, N.H., dated June 24, 1977.\nPink Dolomite: Crystalline cluster from Arkansas, noted as a scarce location, mounted on burgundy felt.\nCondition:\nThe mineral specimens themselves are in natural, raw condition with sharp crystal structures intact. The acrylic display boxes show some typical shelf wear, including light surface scuffs and dust accumulation. Original identification labels are present and legible, though some show minor age-related yellowing. The mounting adhesive and felt backings remain stable.\nOverall Condition\n: All items are USED and are sold AS-IS. Please open a ticket for any questions prior to bidding.\nUsed Item Description\n: Used condition indicates item(s) show signs of regular use, age and may have had repairs or may need repairs. All items featured are DONATED and all sales are FINAL. All BIDS are placed by the buyer with the understanding that this is a donated item that may contain faults unseen by our staff and is ultimately SOLD AS-IS as all information is presented. Items come strictly as pictured and should be assumed to be AS-IS with possible unseen defects. We are\nNOT\nexperts in any field.",
